      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.1 Components of Microsoft Office"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Microsoft Office consists of essential productivity tools including MS Word, MS Excel, and MS PowerPoint.",
        "MS Word covers word processing features and specific components of the MS Word window.",
        "MS Excel focuses on spreadsheet terminology, grid layouts, and common analytical functions.",
        "MS PowerPoint highlights presentation design, slide components, and visual features.",
        "Basic keyboard shortcuts and specific exam points are vital for answering computer awareness questions quickly."
      ],
